-origin-couple-sentenced-in-uk-for-covid-ppe-fraud-millions-spent-on-luxuries/articleshow/135071242.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/indian-origin-couple-sentenced-in-uk-for-covid-ppe-fraud-millions-spent-on-luxuries/articleshow/135071242.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-20T19:21:41+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Trisha Mahajan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135071413,imgsize-384643.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Italian banker was 'dropped to his death by mistake' when thugs dangled him out of his office window 'only to threaten']]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135071580.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/italian-banker-was-dropped-to-his-death-by-mistake-when-thugs-dangled-him-out-of-his-office-window-only-to-threaten/articleshow/135071580.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/italian-banker-was-dropped-to-his-death-by-mistake-when-thugs-dangled-him-out-of-his-office-window-only-to-threaten/articleshow/135071580.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-20T19:35:14+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135071638,imgsize-75630.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Florida couple missed 66 mortgage payments; husband's legal challenge fails after 17 years]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135068652.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A Florida couple missed 66 monthly mortgage payments on their Naples property, triggering a foreclosure dispute that began in 2009. During the legal battle, Gregory Brian Myers agreed to deposit $5,000 monthly while appealing the foreclosure. He later sued U.S. Bank, alleging it had violated their agreement. On October 19, 2026, a federal appeals court upheld the dismissal of his lawsuit.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-florida-couple-missed-66-mortgage-payments-on-their-naples-property-the-husband-later-agreed-to-deposit-5000-monthly-during-an-appeal-but-an-october-19-federal-ruling-rejected-his-lawsuit-against-the-bank/articleshow/135068652.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-florida-couple-missed-66-mortgage-payments-on-their-naples-property-the-husband-later-agreed-to-deposit-5000-monthly-during-an-appeal-but-an-october-19-federal-ruling-rejected-his-lawsuit-against-the-bank/articleshow/135068652.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-20T19:06:17+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135070726,imgsize-192508.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[1867 gold coin found in Texas closet sells for $97,600 after 159 years in a family’s possession]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135069135.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A remarkable 1867-S Liberty Half Eagle gold coin was unearthed from an obscure closet in Texas, boasting a staggering value of $97,600. This highly sought-after coin, a valuable heirloom of a Union soldier, shattered previous auction records. Experts praised its rarity and condition, sparking intense competition among collectors. After a thrilling auction, the coin found its new home in a private collection, bringing its extraordinary journey to a close.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1867-san-francisco-minted-a-5-gold-coin-that-passed-down-through-a-family-159-years-later-it-was-found-inside-a-cigar-box-in-a-texas-closet-and-sold-for-97600-after-experts-identified-its-rarity/articleshow/135069135.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1867-san-francisco-minted-a-5-gold-coin-that-passed-down-through-a-family-159-years-later-it-was-found-inside-a-cigar-box-in-a-texas-closet-and-sold-for-97600-after-experts-identified-its-rarity/articleshow/135069135.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-20T17:24:06+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135069509,imgsize-1403767.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Qing dynasty bowl with bats and peaches sells for $2.048 million after 87 years in a Chicago museum]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135068919.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A stunning porcelain bowl from the Qing dynasty recently fetched $2.048 million at a Christie's auction. Crafted during Emperor Yongzheng's reign, the bowl is adorned with auspicious symbols, hinting it was a birthday gift for the emperor. After decades in the Art Institute of Chicago, the proceeds will fund new acquisitions and conservation efforts. This sale is part of a lucrative two-day auction dedicated to Chinese art.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/between-1723-and-1735-qing-artisans-made-a-porcelain-bowl-painted-with-bats-and-peaches-after-passing-through-a-paris-dealer-and-spending-87-years-at-a-chicago-museum-it-sold-for-2-048-million-in-new-york/articleshow/135068919.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/between-1723-and-1735-qing-artisans-made-a-porcelain-bowl-painted-with-bats-and-peaches-after-passing-through-a-paris-dealer-and-spending-87-years-at-a-chicago-museum-it-sold-for-2-048-million-in-new-york/articleshow/135068919.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-20T17:06:04+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135069046,imgsize-1533713.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[65-year old swimmer killed in shark attack off South African coast; 2 beaches shut]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135070403.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Tragedy struck at Orient Beach in KuGompo City when 65-year-old open-water swimmer Janine Lochrenberg was fatally attacked by a shark. Despite the desperate efforts of fellow swimmers who rushed to assist her, she suffered life-threatening injuries to her arm and thigh, ultimately succumbing to her wounds. In response, local authorities promptly closed the beach and launched an investigation, as reports indicate a slight rise in shark attacks in recent years.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/65-year-old-swimmer-killed-in-shark-attack-off-south-african-coast-2-beaches-shut/articleshow/135070403.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/65-year-old-swimmer-killed-in-shark-attack-off-south-african-coast-2-beaches-shut/articleshow/135070403.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-20T18:19:12+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135070436,imgsize-58638.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Daniel Rotman built PrettyLitter into a brand valued at $1.4 billion before Mars’ buyout]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135067881.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/daniel-rotman-spotted-a-gap-in-the-cat-litter-market-and-built-prettylitter-mars-later-bought-out-his-stake-at-a-reported-1-4-billion-valuation/articleshow/135067881.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/daniel-rotman-spotted-a-gap-in-the-cat-litter-market-and-built-prettylitter-mars-later-bought-out-his-stake-at-a-reported-1-4-billion-valuation/articleshow/135067881.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-20T18:02:02+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135070253,imgsize-23288.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Georgia woman’s deed to stepson rescinded; appeals court upholds $57,600 award]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135067078.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a complex property dispute, a woman in Georgia transferred her property interest to her stepson during a period of cognitive decline. Her guardian, suspecting exploitation and fraud, pursued legal action, leading to a jury decision that invalidated the transfer and awarded damages. The stepson contested this ruling, alleging jury misconduct. However, the appeals court decided to uphold the initial verdict, solidifying the guardian's victory.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2020-a-georgia-woman-transferred-her-interest-in-a-home-to-her-stepson-despite-concerns-about-her-memory-a-jury-later-rescinded-the-deed-and-awarded-57600-in-damages-and-an-october-19-appeals-court-upheld-the-verdict/articleshow/135067078.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2020-a-georgia-woman-transferred-her-interest-in-a-home-to-her-stepson-despite-concerns-about-her-memory-a-jury-later-rescinded-the-deed-and-awarded-57600-in-damages-and-an-october-19-appeals-court-upheld-the-verdict/articleshow/135067078.cms]]></guid><pubDate>